\section{Imports}

Every reader this module needs already exists in \cref{commits}: the
block separator (\cref{sec:block-sep}), the run block parser
(\cref{sec:parse-run-block}, which also delivers the view trace of a
review run, \cref{sec:view-trace}), the exception line
(\cref{sec:parse-exception-line}), the stream prefixes
(\cref{sec:io-stream-prefixes}) and the section splitter
(\cref{sec:split-commit-detail}).
Re-deriving any of them here would mean two parsers for one format,
and the second one would be the one nobody notices is wrong.

[[_parse_iso]] is private to \cref{commits} and imported anyway.
The alternative is a second [[try]]\slash[[except ValueError]] around
[[datetime.fromisoformat]] here, and \enquote{a malformed timestamp is
missing data, not an error} is a decision this package should make once
rather than twice.
[[NO_IO_PLACEHOLDER]] reaches us through the same module: it is
written by \cref{gitrepo} and re-exported by the reader that already
imports it, so the card recognises the placeholder by the writer's own
spelling.

